        },
        "message": "docs(1430): manifest and theme-color readback through Chromium's own parser\n\nThe first-paint evidence had the DOM readback and the manifest file diff but\nno reading by a browser's manifest parser. manifest-cdp.mjs opens the dev\nserver in Chromium (Playwright), stores each theme in localStorage, and asks\nthe browser for its parsed manifest over CDP (Page.getAppManifest); the result\nis manifest-cdp.json: zero parse errors, theme_color and background_color\n#1a1612, and the theme-color metas rewritten to the stored theme's --canvas\n(#f3eee5 light, #1a1612 dark) by theme.ts.\n\nAddress-bar and install-splash screenshots are still not captured: headless\nChromium draws no browser chrome and Safari access was declined on the host.\nIssue #1430 is already closed; this supplements its evidence.",
